Error message: `The Pod "app-68bc7878f-fhlj6" is invalid: spec: Forbidden: pod updates may not change fields other than spec.containers[*].image, spec.initContainers[*].image, spec.activeDeadlineSeconds, spec.tolerations (only additions to existing tolerations), spec.terminationGracePeriodSeconds (allow it to be set to 1 if it was previously negative)`

This confirms that pod configurations like resource limits cannot be patched directly on a running pod; they must be changed in the controller (ReplicaSet, Deployment, or Job template).

The pod was created by a `ReplicaSet/app-68bc7878f`. This is the persistent resource that owns the faulty state. I must patch the ReplicaSet to update the template.

I need to patch the ReplicaSet `app-68bc7878f` in the `default` namespace.

The patch structure for a ReplicaSet/Deployment template is similar to the pod structure, but I need to target `.spec.template.spec.containers[0].resources.limits`.

I will use a JSON patch to add the limits and also add requests to be safe, as often setting limits without requests causes scheduling issues.

Target: `app-68bc7878f` ReplicaSet, `default` namespace.
Path: `/spec/template/spec/containers/0/resources` (adding the whole resources object)

I will apply the patch to the ReplicaSet.

```bash
kubectl patch replicaset app-68bc7878f -n default --type=merge --patch '
{
  "spec": {
    "template": {
      "spec": {
        "containers": [
          {
            "name": "app",
            "resources": {
              "limits": {
                "cpu": "100m",
                "memory": "64Mi"
              },
              "requests": {
                "cpu": "100m",
                "memory": "64Mi"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}'
```
I will use strategic merge patch (`--type=merge`) since it handles nested objects like this better than a simple JSON path operation on a complex resource like a ReplicaSet.

After patching the ReplicaSet, Kubernetes will roll out a new ReplicaSet, which will create new Pods with the correct configuration. The old pods will be terminated. I must wait for the new pods to reach the "Ready" state.

The API rejected the patch again, this time complaining about `spec.template.spec.containers[0].image: Required value`. This suggests that while I was modifying the resources, I either accidentally omitted the `image` field or the merge patch logic somehow invalidated the required field.

Since I used `--type=merge` and provided a partial definition for the container, I must ensure all required fields, especially the `image`, are present and unchanged, or I must use a JSON patch that only modifies the specific path for resources while preserving the existing structure.

Given the complexity of the error and the need to preserve the original state, I will revert to a JSON patch that only targets the `resources` field within the container definition, using the full path, ensuring minimal change.

Original container path: `/spec/template/spec/containers/0`
Target field: `/resources`

I will use a JSON patch to replace the existing (null/empty) `resources` object with the new one.

```json
[
  {
    "op": "replace",
    "path": "/spec/template/spec/containers/0/resources",
    "value": {
      "limits": {
        "cpu": "100m",
        "memory": "64Mi"
      },
      "requests": {
        "cpu": "100m",
        "memory": "64Mi"
      }
    }
  }
]
```

I will apply this JSON patch to the ReplicaSet `app-68bc7878f`.

